{"number":1,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-A1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Controls convert every generated or regenerable clickable Border from the write-once Border.name to the freely-mutable AutomationProperties.AutomationId, following the documented in-project pattern (MaterialsControls.automationId, MaterialsControls.fs:139-146): LibraryControls.leafRow (Border.name at LibraryControls.fs:112) and LibraryControls.actionButton (:148) — the live Selector-bay crash 'Cannot set Name : styled element already styled' — plus the latent copies RotationControls.clickBox (RotationControls.fs:119), RayPositionControls.clickBox (RayPositionControls.fs:71), ElementPaletteControls.clickBox (ElementPaletteControls.fs:55), and ExperimentControls.optionBoxV / actionButton (ExperimentControls.fs:240,581 — the module already documents the AutomationId precedent at :261-266). Key every variable-membership generated list item with View.withKey. NO behaviour change: labels, layout, handlers, and message flow stay identical; headless tests that located these controls by Name switch to AutomationProperties.GetAutomationId.","acceptance":"After the sweep, no generated or regenerable row/box in OpticalConstructor.Controls sets StyledElement.Name; a headless test drives the Selector bay through select, bind, and kind-change re-renders without a styled-element rename throw; every existing headless test still locates its controls.","section":"Part A — FuncUI dynamic-list hygiene (CRITICAL — land first)"}
{"number":2,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Retire the dead Elmish shell — the composition comment records the old constructor shell is kept but no longer opened by the launcher Main button (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:112-117). Delete the MainWindow host type and the Startup.localizationError surface from OpticalConstructor.App (Program.fs:36-110), and delete from OpticalConstructor.Ui the shell modules Shell.fs, Ribbon.fs, MaterialsView.fs, ConstructionPage.fs, ConstructorView.fs, LifecycleView.fs, Templates.fs, Help.fs plus every Ui module left without a live consumer by those deletions (delete transitively until nothing dead remains; verify by build). KEEP UserEnvironment.fs (live at Program.fs:37) and keep the theme seam App.Initialize uses (AppShell.themeVariant, Program.fs:244) by retaining or relocating that function into a small surviving module. Delete the Ui.Tests tests that pinned the deleted shell behaviour.","acceptance":"After the retirement, OpticalConstructor.App has no MainWindow shell host, the launcher still opens the Main constructor scene, environment.json settings still load and apply the persisted theme, the dead shell modules and their tests are gone, and the solution builds warning-clean.","section":"Part B — Relocation: the workbench moves home"}
{"number":3,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-B2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"REAL-MOVE the workbench from OpticalConstructor.TestWindows into OpticalConstructor.Ui (no file-linking; one fsproj per folder; namespaces become OpticalConstructor.Ui): TableAndElementRotationView.fs, TableScene.fs, SceneInput.fs, Catalogue.fs, ElementRenderer.fs, MaterialEditorView.fs/MaterialEditorWindow.fs, SampleEditorView.fs/SampleEditorWindow.fs, CategoryEditorView.fs/CategoryEditorWindow.fs, NkDispersionChart.fs. The diagnostic scene views/windows (TableRotation, ElementRotation, ElementMovement, RendererTest, SnapToBeam, SnapToReflected, TableAndElementRotationWindow) STAY in OpticalConstructor.TestWindows, which gains a project reference to OpticalConstructor.Ui and opens the moved namespaces. Order the moved files in the Ui fsproj after UserEnvironment.fs. OpticalConstructor.App already references Ui; update its opens. Ui.Tests drive the same views under the new namespaces. The move MUST NOT reintroduce MSB3277 or any our-code warning.","acceptance":"After the move, the workbench modules compile inside OpticalConstructor.Ui under OpticalConstructor.Ui namespaces, OpticalConstructor.TestWindows holds only the diagnostic scenes and references Ui, the launcher Main and all seven test windows still open, and build plus both test suites are green with no new warnings."}
{"number":4,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-B3","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0007","name":"TestLauncherWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App","touches":["OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3],"how_to":"Create the new executable project Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App (net10.0, x64, WinExe — mirror OpticalConstructor.App.fsproj's Avalonia package set; add it to Berreman.slnx) hosting TestLauncherWindow: its own Avalonia Application + entry point and one button per diagnostic scene currently on the product launcher (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:177-224 — Table Rotations, Element Rotations, Table + Element Rotations, Element Movement, Renderers, Snap to Beam, Snap to Reflected), each with a stable Name and AutomationId. Then REMOVE those seven buttons from the product LauncherWindow and DROP OpticalConstructor.App's project reference to OpticalConstructor.TestWindows — test code leaves the product dependency graph; the product launcher keeps Main only (Inverse/Materials/Library land in step 45). Ui.Tests references the new project and renders the window headless.","acceptance":"After the step, OpticalConstructor.TestWindows.App builds as its own executable whose TestLauncherWindow renders all seven scene buttons under a headless frame, and OpticalConstructor.App no longer references OpticalConstructor.TestWindows while its launcher still opens Main."}
{"number":5,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Introduce appsettings.json read/written ONLY through Softellect.Sys.AppSettings.AppSettingsProvider (Softellect.Sys 10.1.301.54, already referenced by OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj; add the same package reference to OpticalConstructor.App). Create the provider ONCE at the composition root via AppSettingsProvider.tryCreate () — its SetOnMissing behaviour writes every missing key's default back so the first run self-documents. Add ONE [<RequireQualifiedAccess>] ConfigKey module of [<Literal>] key constants beside the provider read in OpticalConstructor.App; initial inventory: SelectWindowsModal (default false), QuickPickThreshold (5), TreeAutoBuildThreshold (100), ThicknessBucketCap (8), plus the connectionStrings entries and DB provider key consumed by step 40. Typed values flow inward as a pure Domain settings record (new module, e.g. OpticalConstructor.Domain/WorkbenchSettings.fs) of elevated types: SelectWindowModality = ModalSelectWindows | ModelessSelectWindows (never a naked bool) and QuickPickThreshold / TreeAutoBuildThreshold / ThicknessBucketCap as single-case DUs with .value plus tryCreate rejecting non-positive values — no view or Domain module ever reads the provider ambiently. appsettings.json is a build-copied content item of OpticalConstructor.App; user preferences REMAIN in environment.json — the two never merge. Unit tests construct the settings record directly and cover defaults and tryCreate rejection without touching disk.","acceptance":"After the step, the app creates/opens appsettings.json through AppSettingsProvider with the four defaults written back on first run, the Domain settings record carries only elevated types with tryCreate validation, and unit tests prove the defaults path with no file IO.","section":"Part C — appsettings, app-scoped composition, and the WindowLauncher seam"}
{"number":6,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-C2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3],"how_to":"Hoist proxy construction out of the MainConstructorWindow constructor (OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:129-147) into ONE app-scope composition value built at startup before any window opens: a record (the *Context convention) bundling the five proxies — LibraryProxy, ExperimentProxy, MaterialProxy, SampleProxy, CategoryProxy — plus the step-5 settings record, injected into MainConstructorWindow and every window opened later, so launcher-opened and constructor-opened windows share the same in-memory stores. The parameterless DefaultStores composition (Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs after step 3's move; today at TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:270-280) stays the test-scene default. Headless test: two surfaces composed from the app scope observe the same store — a material added through one is listed by the other.","acceptance":"After the step, the five proxies are created exactly once at startup and injected into every window, and a headless test proves two surfaces over the app scope share one store."}
{"number":7,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-C3","id":"SVC_XDUO_0001","name":"WindowLauncher","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Ui","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,5],"how_to":"Declare in OpticalConstructor.Ui the window-opening seam, generalizing the EditorLaunchers function-record precedent (today at TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:116-141, in Ui after step 3): a WindowKey DU naming every managed window — MaterialsWindowKey, LibraryWindowKey, SolverHandoffWindowKey, CategoryEditorKey, and id-keyed editor keys MaterialEditorKey of MaterialId / SampleEditorKey of SampleId; EntryFreshness = NewUnsaved | Persisted (new entities mint their Guid at Add-window open so the registry keys uniformly by id from the first moment); and the [<ReferenceEquality>] record WindowLauncher of camelCase Result-returning functions that open-or-activate a window for a key (create through an injected per-key window factory when absent, activate the live window when present, re-target an existing Select-state window per step 16), forget a key on close, and decide Select-state modality from the step-5 SelectWindowModality. Provide a mock (stub factories recording calls) plus a mock-driven Ui.Tests test exercising every field through its exact signature.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven headless test MUST build a stub WindowLauncher and observe that a second open of the same WindowKey activates instead of creating, two different editor keys create two windows, and every record field is exercised through its exact signature; it passes."}
{"number":8,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-C3","id":"SVC_XDUO_0001","name":"WindowLauncher","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[6,7],"how_to":"Implement the real launcher over a WindowRegistry: module-level mutable Map<WindowKey, Window> held at the HOST layer, outside any Elmish model (the registered-storage-provider host-seam pattern, OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:96 in today's tree — that shell line is retired by step 2). Activate = Window.Activate on the registered live window; create = invoke the injected factory, register, unregister on Closed. Editor windows key by the edited entity's id: an Add-opened editor mints MaterialId.create () / SampleId.create () AT WINDOW OPEN and carries EntryFreshness = NewUnsaved — moving the id-mint off the save path (newMaterialId at MaterialEditorView.fs:416 pre-move and the SampleEditorWindow add path) — with Save routing addMaterial/addSample for NewUnsaved and updateMaterial/updateSample for Persisted. Select-state opens honor ModalSelectWindows via ShowDialog with the requesting window as owner, ModelessSelectWindows via Show; Browse windows always Show. Rewire the workbench Add/Edit/Categories verbs through the launcher, subsuming EditorLaunchers.defaults. Headless tests: Edit of the same material twice activates one window; Add twice creates two NewUnsaved windows with distinct upfront Guids; Save of a NewUnsaved editor persists through addMaterial.","acceptance":"After the step, opening the same entity's editor twice MUST activate the existing window, a new entity MUST carry its upfront-minted Guid and NewUnsaved freshness from open through Save (addMaterial/addSample), and Select-state modality follows the appsettings switch — all verified headless."}
{"number":9,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Create OpticalConstructor.Domain/Facets.fs — pure, Avalonia-free. Types: AttributeKey and DiscreteKey single-case string DUs with .value; AttributeValue = DiscreteValue of DiscreteKey | NumericValue of double; Applicability = ApplicableAttribute | InapplicableAttribute; AttributeKind = DiscreteAttribute | NumericAttribute; AttributeDef<'item> = { key : AttributeKey; name : string; kind : AttributeKind; appliesTo : 'item -> Applicability; extract : 'item -> AttributeValue list } (extract returns a LIST — multi-valued facets are first-class); FacetSelection = DiscreteSelection of Set<DiscreteKey> (OR within a facet) | NumericRangeSelection of a lower/upper pair; AppliedConstraint = { key : AttributeKey; selection : FacetSelection }; Representation = an ordered AttributeKey list. Engine functions with explicit concrete signatures, all naive folds (corpus is tens to hundreds; no indices): filter (defs, applied constraints, items to items — AND across facets, OR within one), countFor (count-preview of one candidate constraint under the applied set), breadcrumb after-counts (the cumulative result count after each applied constraint in application order), and buildTree (representation, defs, constraints, items to a FacetTree whose branches carry value label + count, zero-count branches dropped, inapplicable attributes omitted entirely); a plain-text filter participates as an ordinary constraint over a caller-supplied text extractor. Unit tests in OpticalConstructor.Tests cover every function including multi-valued extraction, where branch counts need not sum to the total.","acceptance":"After the step, pure unit tests MUST prove filter, countFor, and buildTree over a fixed corpus: OR within a facet, AND across facets, multi-valued attributes counted per branch, zero-count branches absent, inapplicable attributes absent, and cumulative breadcrumb after-counts in application order.","section":"Part D — The faceted engine (Domain, pure)"}
{"number":10,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[9],"how_to":"Add the numeric bucket builder every NumericAttribute branch uses (in Facets.fs or a sibling FacetBuckets module): bucket boundaries from the 1-2-5 log ladder spanning the CURRENTLY CONSTRAINED population's min/max; empty buckets dropped; adjacent buckets merged fewest-items-first while the bucket count exceeds ThicknessBucketCap (step 5, default 8); half-open [lo, hi) intervals; a single distinct value collapses to one exact-value bucket; display labels like '10-20 nm (7)' using nm below 1 µm and µm at or above; buckets recomputed on every constraint change; a manual min-max entry applies as an ordinary NumericRangeSelection constraint chip, never a special path. Unit tests: ladder boundary generation, fewest-first merge order under the cap, half-open edge membership, single-value collapse, nm/µm label switch, and recomputation under a narrowed population; an FsCheck property that every item lands in exactly one bucket.","acceptance":"After the step, pure tests MUST prove the 1-2-5 ladder boundaries, fewest-first merging to the cap, half-open membership, exact-value collapse, unit-switched labels, and the exactly-one-bucket property."}
{"number":11,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-D3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[9,10],"how_to":"Add the two concrete facet catalogues as data (new Domain module, e.g. LibraryFacets.fs). MATERIAL facets (extractors over MaterialEntry — MaterialLibrary.fs:230-238; complexity is None for coded presets): Category (corpus-derived from the seeded catalogue, standardCategories MaterialLibrary.fs:118); Anisotropy (Isotropic/Uniaxial/Biaxial); Constant-vs-dispersive; Transparent-vs-absorbing offered for CONSTANT materials only (appliesTo); Dispersion model — MULTI-VALUED per axis/segment over the DispersionModel cases (DispersionModels.fs:168-178) so counts need not sum to the total; optical activity to symmetry class and handedness, offered only when active, the classes via availableGyrationClasses (MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:373), never re-derived; magnetic to scalar/gyromagnetic, only when magnetic. LIBRARY-ENTRY facets (LibraryEntry, ElementId.fs:188-192): the kind facet always; every material facet lifted to samples as the DISTINCT UNION over constituent materials (substrate plus film layers — any constituent matches); substrate material offered only for Plate/Wedge; 'has thin films' derived from structure.films non-empty independent of SubstrateKind; film material(s) corpus-derived, name-sorted, multiselect; per-film thickness as a NumericAttribute bucketed by step 10. Unit tests pin each extractor and each appliesTo rule over the seeded corpora (builtInEntries, SeedSamples).","acceptance":"After the step, tests MUST prove dependent facets vanish entirely when inapplicable, the dispersion-model facet is multi-valued, sample facets match on any constituent material, and per-film thickness values flow into the step-10 buckets."}
{"number":12,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-E1","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0008","name":"FacetedTreeControls","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Controls","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[9,10],"how_to":"Create OpticalConstructor.Controls/FacetedTreeControls.fs, domain-free (the MaterialsControls State+Handlers shape): a pure State record (the built tree, applied-constraint breadcrumbs with labels and after-counts, offered values with count-previews, named representations plus the active one, the text-filter draft, the live result count, and a materialization mode) and a Handlers record of unit-returning functions (applyConstraint, removeConstraint, commitTextFilter, chooseRepresentation, requestBuild, selectNode, applyManualRange). Render: a breadcrumb strip of removable chips each showing its after-count; the live result count; a Show/Search button INSTEAD of tree rows whenever State says materialization is gated (result count above TreeAutoBuildThreshold); branch rows showing 'label (count)' with unexpanded branches carrying their counts; everything in a ScrollViewer (the tree may span pages). The text filter commits on Enter/LostFocus ONLY — never per keystroke. Every generated row is keyed with View.withKey and carries AutomationProperties.AutomationId, never StyledElement.Name; ids are intent-named [<Literal>] constants. The control renders exactly what it is given and never touches a proxy or the facet engine — the host projects Domain state in. Headless Ui.Tests: mount over a known State, find every id, assert chip click dispatches removeConstraint, offered-value click dispatches applyConstraint, gated mode shows the button and zero tree rows, and typing does not dispatch per keystroke.","acceptance":"After the step, a headless test MUST mount FacetedTreeControls over a known State, locate every declared automation id, observe apply/remove/build handler dispatch, and confirm the filter box never commits per keystroke.","section":"Part E — FacetedTree control and the Materials window"}
{"number":13,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-E2","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0009","name":"MaterialsWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Ui","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[8,11,12],"how_to":"Create the single-instance Materials WINDOW in OpticalConstructor.Ui: a HostWindow mounting an MVU model that projects MaterialProxy + CategoryProxy through the step-11 material facets into FacetedTreeControls state, beside a view panel (selected entry metadata plus the embeddable dual-axis n/k chart, Controls/EmbeddedChart.fs) and the existing verbs Add / Edit / Remove / Categories… rewired to this window — Add/Edit/Categories through the step-8 WindowLauncher editor keys, Remove keeping its inline confirm gate and the typed MaterialStillReferenced block. REMOVE the Materials bay from the ribbon: drop materialsBay from mainBays (Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs after the move; today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2339) and its BayNames entry; the ribbon tab-strip row gains a right-aligned 'Materials…' button opening the window through WindowLauncher (MaterialsWindowKey) — the constructor-side entry point (the launcher button lands in step 45). Thread the window factory into the App composition mechanically so the solution builds (step 47 owns the composition acceptance). After every verb the window re-queries its proxies in the same render pass. Stable intent-named ids for the window, strip button, tree host, view panel, and verbs. Headless tests: the strip button opens ONE window (second click activates), applying facet constraints narrows the corpus, verbs operate over the shared app-scoped stores, and a category rename re-labels the category facet.","acceptance":"After the step, the Materials bay is gone from the ribbon and the 'Materials…' strip button opens a single-instance Materials window whose faceted tree, view panel, and Add/Edit/Remove/Categories… verbs operate over the shared stores — verified headless."}
{"number":14,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-F1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"In OpticalConstructor.Domain make ideal elements ordinary protected entries and polarizer behaviour data. EntryProtection = ProtectedBuiltIn | UserManaged, exposed by every LibraryEntry (ElementId.fs:188-192): the seeded presets src-600 / det-intensity / det-ellipsometer / pol-lp / pol-cp-left / pol-cp-right (seedEntries, ElementId.fs:532-541) are ProtectedBuiltIn; samples (seeded and user-created) are UserManaged. PolarizerBehavior = ComputedIdeal of PolarizerKind | ConstantMueller of MuellerComponent list with MuellerComponent = { matrix : MuellerMatrix; offset : Angle } — components stored at reference orientation, rotated at run time R(-theta)*M*R(theta), the compound evaluated as the ORDERED product on demand; PolarizerCategory = LpCategory | CpCategory | LpCpCategory | CpLpCategory | CustomMueller as the polarizer facet value. PolarizerPreset (ElementId.fs:179-184) carries behavior + category; the three seeded ideals become ComputedIdeal entries that synthesize through the EXISTING Propagation.inputStokes / analyzerMueller (Propagation.fs:54-89) exactly as today. ConstantMueller entries evaluate ONLY in the Stokes/Mueller pipeline — they never enter the Berreman stack; the dedicated editor for ConstantMueller entries is OUT OF SCOPE (the DU makes it a non-breaking future addition). Unit tests: ComputedIdeal matrices equal Propagation.analyzerMueller across sampled orientations; a two-component ConstantMueller (two linear polarizers at different offsets) multiplies in order with each component rotated by its offset; every seeded preset reports ProtectedBuiltIn and every seeded sample UserManaged.","acceptance":"After the step, tests MUST prove ComputedIdeal parity with the existing analyzer synthesis across orientations, ordered rotated-product evaluation for a ConstantMueller compound, and ProtectedBuiltIn on every seeded preset with seeded samples UserManaged.","section":"Part F — Library window; ideal elements become protected entries"}
{"number":15,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-F2","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0010","name":"LibraryWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Ui","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[8,11,12,14],"how_to":"Create the single-instance Library WINDOW in OpticalConstructor.Ui over the WHOLE LibraryEntry corpus — samples, sources, polarizers, detectors (LibraryProxy, ElementId.fs:276-281, plus SampleProxy for the sample verbs) — through FacetedTreeControls with the seeded default representation 'By kind': the kind facet first, the step-11 sample facets on the sample subtree, and the PolarizerCategory facet on polarizers. Verbs rewired from the Library bay: Add sample / Make multilayer / Edit / Remove as today (editors through WindowLauncher; Remove keeps its confirm gate and typed blocks and REFUSES a ProtectedBuiltIn entry with a typed reason). REMOVE the Library bay (samplesBay from mainBays — today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:2340 — and its BayNames entry) and add the right-aligned 'Library…' strip button through WindowLauncher (LibraryWindowKey); thread the window factory into the App composition mechanically (step 47 owns the composition acceptance). Stable intent-named ids. Headless tests: single-instance behaviour, the by-kind tree lists every entry kind with counts, sample verbs operate over the shared stores, and Remove on a protected entry surfaces the typed refusal and changes nothing.","acceptance":"After the step, the Library bay is gone, the 'Library…' strip button opens a single-instance Library window whose by-kind faceted tree lists every entry kind with counts and whose verbs work over the shared stores, and removing a protected entry is refused with a typed message — verified headless."}
{"number":16,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-G1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[13,15],"how_to":"Give BOTH windows the mode DU — the same window in code, never a copy. In Domain: KindConstraint (the constrained CatalogueKind), SelectionTarget = TableElementTarget of ElementId | SampleLayerTarget of LayerPosition, SelectionContext = { constraint : KindConstraint; target : SelectionTarget; onSelected : selected-entry callback; onCancelled : unit callback }, LibraryWindowMode = Browse | Select of SelectionContext. In Select state the window pre-applies the kind constraint as NON-REMOVABLE (no breadcrumb chip) and adds exactly TWO buttons in one row with distinct positive/negative styling — 'Select' (returns the highlighted entry through onSelected, then closes) and 'Close' (onCancelled) — everything else IS the ordinary window, so add-on-the-fly works because it is the library. WindowLauncher opens Select-state windows modal or modeless per the step-5 switch, and a second Select open RE-TARGETS the existing single instance. Staleness rules (modeless default): a changed table selection or the target's disappearance cancels and closes the open Select window (the pending-bind-clears precedent — today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:941-944); a second Choose closes the first; onSelected dispatches a TARGETED message and a vanished target is a no-op plus a status line, never a throw. Headless tests: Select state shows the two buttons and the non-removable constraint; Select returns the entry and closes; a selection change closes the window; a vanished target no-ops with a status line.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST prove the Select/Close pair, the pre-applied non-removable kind constraint, targeted onSelected dispatch, close-on-selection-change, and the vanished-target no-op for both windows' Select states.","section":"Part G — Select mode, Selector flow, pre-binding, sample-editor picking"}
{"number":17,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-G2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[5,16],"how_to":"Rework the Selector bay flow: with an element selected, a 'Choose…' verb opens the Library window in Select state constrained to the element's kind (through WindowLauncher). The inline quick-pick strip — today's kind-constrained rows plus confirm panel via LibraryControls — renders ONLY when the kind-constrained entry count is below QuickPickThreshold (step 5, default 5); at or above the threshold the bay shows Choose… alone. BOTH paths converge on the SAME bind message that commits placement.valueId (today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:768,780). Stable ids for Choose… and the strip. Headless tests: an over-threshold kind shows Choose… and no strip; an under-threshold kind shows the strip; binding through the strip and through the Select window land the identical valueId.","acceptance":"After the step, the quick-pick strip renders only below the threshold, Choose… opens the kind-constrained Select-state Library window, and both paths commit the identical valueId bind — verified headless."}
{"number":18,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-G3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,14],"how_to":"Pre-bind every new table element except a sample to its seeded default: the palette add path binds LightSource to src-600 and Detector to det-intensity (seed ids, ElementId.fs:535-540), and the polarizer palette exposes THREE add buttons — LP (pol-lp), CPL (pol-cp-left), CPR (pol-cp-right) — with CatalogueKind UNCHANGED (LP maps to LinearPolarizer, CPL/CPR to CircularPolarizer — Placement.fs:93-101): only the palette label and the pre-bound entry differ. ElementPaletteControls grows the two extra polarizer buttons with stable ids. Samples stay UNBOUND — that is the inverse hook. RETIRE the silent ideal-analyzer fallback: replace the Option.defaultValue Library.IdealLinear tail of runAnalyzerKind (today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:1407-1427) with reading the bound polarizer entry's kind; when the scene holds NO bound polarizer the experiment surface reports a typed 'no analyzer present' status instead of silently assuming an ideal linear analyzer. Headless/unit tests: each palette add lands pre-bound to its seed id; a new sample is unbound; the three polarizer buttons map to the unchanged kinds; no code path defaults to IdealLinear silently.","acceptance":"After the step, adding a source/detector/LP/CPL/CPR element lands pre-bound to its seeded entry while a new sample stays unbound, the palette shows three polarizer buttons over unchanged CatalogueKinds, and the silent IdealLinear fallback no longer exists — verified by headless and unit tests."}
{"number":19,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-G4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[16],"how_to":"Replace the sample editor's WrapPanel material picker (today TestWindows/SampleEditorView.fs:740-758) with a per-layer 'Choose material…' verb opening the MATERIALS window in Select state targeted at that LayerPosition (step-16 SelectionContext with SampleLayerTarget; the staleness rules apply — a deleted row makes the return a no-op plus status line). The editor RE-QUERIES MaterialProxy.listMaterials whenever a Select window returns and on window activation, replacing the load-once snapshot (today TestWindows/SampleEditorWindow.fs:32-35); live cross-window notifications are OUT OF SCOPE. The by-MaterialId selection contract (ChooseMaterial) is unchanged. Headless tests: Choose material… opens the Materials window in Select state targeted at the row; the returned selection binds that row's material; deleting the row first makes the return a no-op; a material added through another window appears after activation re-query.","acceptance":"After the step, the sample editor picks materials through the Materials window's Select state targeted by LayerPosition with vanished-row no-op, and its material list refreshes on Select-return and window activation — verified headless."}
{"number":20,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-H1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"New Domain module (e.g. OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs): VersionNumber single-case int DU with .value, .next, and a first value; MaterialVersionId = { materialId : MaterialId; version : VersionNumber }; SampleVersionId = { sampleId : SampleId; version : VersionNumber }; EntryLifecycle = ActiveEntry | InactiveEntry; VersionRef = MaterialVersionRef of MaterialVersionId | SampleVersionRef of SampleVersionId; and the used-seam record VersionsInUse = { versionsInUse : unit -> Set<VersionRef> } (computed from the in-memory experiment store by step 25; truthful later when persistence arrives). Express the version-creation rule ONCE as a pure decision function shared by both stores: inputs are the stored latest version's physics payload, the incoming save (physics + metadata), and whether that version is used; output a DU MutateInPlace | MintNextVersion | KeepCurrent — an unused version mutates in place, a used version with STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT physics mints the next, an identical physics save keeps the current version, and metadata-only edits (name, description, category) NEVER version regardless of use. Unit tests enumerate the used/unused x physics-changed/identical x metadata-only decision table.","acceptance":"After the step, pure tests MUST prove the decision table: unused edits mutate in place, used physics changes mint the next version, identical saves keep the version, and metadata-only edits never version.","section":"Part H — Lifecycle: versioning, supersede, active/inactive"}
{"number":21,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-H2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[20],"how_to":"Re-shape the registered MaterialProxy (STORE_XDUO_0001) IN PLACE — same record name, kind, and declaring project (MaterialLibrary.fs:506; createInMemory ElementId.fs:722); no temporary, no shim (spec-md 0.2). The store becomes versions per MaterialId: listMaterials lists LATEST ACTIVE versions with an explicit include-inactive switch (a two-case DU, not a bool) for the show-inactive toggle; a by-MaterialVersionId resolve serves reference resolution and IGNORES lifecycle; saveMaterial applies the step-20 decision function against the injected VersionsInUse (mutate / mint next / keep); metadata edits update in place on every version-decision branch; lifecycle verbs markMaterialInactive / markMaterialActive / supersedeMaterial (a superseded version behaves as inactive automatically); removeMaterial keeps the MaterialStillReferenced hard-block (ElementId.fs:755-765) and ADDITIONALLY refuses any material with a used version via a new typed MaterialError case carrying the reason. The library edits the LATEST version only; older versions are view-only resolution targets. Update every consumer mechanically (bays/windows/editors list latest-active; facets unchanged in behaviour). Tests: version growth per the decision table over a stubbed VersionsInUse, latest-active default listing, inactive hidden from offers yet resolvable by version, supersede behaving as inactive, and both removal blocks.","acceptance":"After the step, MaterialProxy exposes versioned save/resolve/lifecycle with the shared decision rule enforced, default listing returns latest active versions, used versions are un-deletable with typed refusals, and all consumers compile with tests green."}
{"number":22,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-H3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[20,21],"how_to":"Mirror step 21 for the registered SampleProxy (STORE_XDUO_0002, ElementId.fs:318; createInMemory :652), in place: versions per SampleId, saveSample through the SAME step-20 decision function with VersionsInUse, latest-active listing with the include-inactive switch, by-SampleVersionId resolve ignoring lifecycle, lifecycle verbs, and removal hard-blocks extended to used versions. ALSO re-type the material references a sample carries to VERSIONS (spec-md Part H: references point at a version): SampleStructure's substrate/film material ids (ElementId.fs:103; builders filmStructure/plateStructure :329,337) become MaterialVersionId, the seeds pinning version one of the seeded materials, and resolution flowing through step 21's by-version resolve. Update the stack editor, sample editor, facet extractors, and every other consumer mechanically. Tests: the step-21 suite mirrored for samples plus a sample-layer version-pin round-trip (a layer keeps resolving its pinned material version after the material mints a newer one).","acceptance":"After the step, SampleProxy is versioned under the shared decision rule, sample layers pin MaterialVersionId (seeds at version one) and keep resolving their pinned version after the material evolves, and all consumers compile with tests green."}
{"number":23,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-H4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[13,15,21,22],"how_to":"Surface lifecycle in BOTH windows: verbs Mark inactive / Mark active / Supersede… on the selected entry, confirm-gated inline, each block a typed inline message; ProtectedBuiltIn library entries expose NO lifecycle verbs (removed, not greyed). A 'show inactive/superseded' toggle (default hidden) adds them to the tree and counts with a visible badge. Pickers, Select mode, and default facet counts EXCLUDE inactive and superseded entries; resolution of existing references ignores lifecycle (the table keeps drawing a bound inactive entry). The view panel lists an entry's versions; older versions open VIEW-ONLY (no Save path); the library always edits the latest. Headless tests: marking an entry inactive removes it from Select offers while its bound reference still resolves on the table; a protected entry shows no lifecycle verbs; the toggle reveals badged inactive entries; an older version opens read-only.","acceptance":"After the step, headless tests MUST prove inactive/superseded exclusion from offers with references still resolving, no lifecycle verbs on protected entries, the badged show-inactive toggle, and view-only older versions."}
{"number":24,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-I1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[],"how_to":"Rename the OLD toggle-based Groups.ExperimentCollection (Groups.fs:114-129) to WorkbenchToggleSet — a TYPE rename only: the GroupsLibrary record (Groups.fs:144-148) and its persisted groups JSON shape are unchanged (the type name never appears in the JSON), and the Storage load/save in OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs re-points mechanically. After this step 'experiment collection' names the live constructor concept exclusively (the Experiments module's collection — its commit at ElementId.fs:1010). Update every reference and test.","acceptance":"After the step, no type named Groups.ExperimentCollection exists, WorkbenchToggleSet round-trips the same groups JSON, and the only ExperimentCollection type in the tree is the live Experiments one — build and tests green.","section":"Part I — Experiments hold the full setup; scene/collection proxies"}
{"number":25,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-I2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[20,21,22,24],"how_to":"Grow Experiments.Experiment (ElementId.fs:909-917) into a FULL setup: an ordered setup list of ElementDescriptor records — each carrying the CatalogueKind, a placement/orientation summary, and the bound entry reference BY VERSION where versioned (a step-20 VersionRef for sample/material-backed bindings; protected presets bind by entry id) — with the varied element identified WITHIN the list, replacing the single elementId/elementLabel pair. Sample and light source are OPTIONAL: E1 = source+polarizer+sample+rotating polarizer, E2 = the same without a sample, and E3 = an empty dark-line setup are all constructible. The detector kind is part of the chain and determines the expected data-file shape (consumed by step 34). Declare DataFilePath (single-case elevated path DU, .value at the IO boundary) and an optional per-experiment attachment slot dataFileOpt : DataFilePath option. The Experiments bay builds descriptors from the live scene on commit (ElementId.fs:1010). Implement the step-20 VersionsInUse over the experiment store's descriptors and inject it into the step-21/22 saves. Update ExperimentProxy and seedExperiments (ElementId.fs:1076-1094) mechanically. Tests: E1/E2/E3 construct and describe; a bound version appears in versionsInUse and unlocks the used-version rules; committing from a scene captures the ordered chain including the detector kind.","acceptance":"After the step, an Experiment carries an ordered descriptor setup with optional sample and source, dark-line experiments construct, commit captures the live chain with versioned bindings, and versionsInUse reflects descriptor references — unit-verified."}
{"number":26,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-I3","id":"STORE_XDUO_0004","name":"SceneProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[21,22],"how_to":"Declare in OpticalConstructor.Domain the scene persistence seam (the LibraryProxy functional-proxy convention, ElementId.fs:276): SceneName single-case string DU with .value and tryCreate rejecting a blank; SceneSnapshot — a pure record capturing the constructor scene as data (elements with id, CatalogueKind, placement, zoom, and valueId binding; the view state; the snap flag); SceneStoreError = InvalidScene of reason : string; and [<ReferenceEquality>] SceneProxy = { saveScene : SceneName -> SceneSnapshot -> Result<unit, SceneStoreError>; tryLoadScene : SceneName -> Result<SceneSnapshot option, SceneStoreError>; listScenes : unit -> Result<SceneName list, SceneStoreError> }. NO disk format and NO .ocproj wiring — the proxy is the seam a future storage cycle swaps. Provide a mock (an inline stub over a fixed map) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising every field through its exact signature.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub SceneProxy and exercise saveScene, tryLoadScene, and listScenes through their exact signatures; it passes."}
{"number":27,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-I3","id":"STORE_XDUO_0004","name":"SceneProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[26],"how_to":"Implement SceneProxy.createInMemory closing over a ref Map<SceneName, SceneSnapshot> (the SampleProxy.createInMemory precedent, ElementId.fs:652): saveScene validates the name (blank yields InvalidScene) and upserts; tryLoadScene and listScenes read the map. Add the pure capture/restore pair in the workbench host: captureScene projecting the live model's elements, bindings, and view state into a SceneSnapshot, and restoreScene applying a snapshot back onto a model — both pure and unit-testable without a window. Round-trip unit tests: capture, save, load, restore reproduces element ids, kinds, placements, bindings, and view state over deterministic data.","acceptance":"After the step, createInMemory round-trips capture-save-load-restore reproducing element ids, kinds, placements, bindings, and view state — unit-verified with deterministic data."}
{"number":28,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-I4","id":"STORE_XDUO_0005","name":"ExperimentCollectionProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[25],"how_to":"Declare in OpticalConstructor.Domain the experiment-collection persistence seam: CollectionName single-case string DU with .value and tryCreate rejecting a blank; ExperimentCollectionSnapshot = { name : CollectionName; experiments : Experiment list } over the step-25 full-setup experiments (each carrying its optional DataFilePath attachment); ExperimentCollectionError = InvalidCollection of reason : string; and [<ReferenceEquality>] ExperimentCollectionProxy = { saveCollection : ExperimentCollectionSnapshot -> Result<unit, ExperimentCollectionError>; tryLoadCollection : CollectionName -> Result<ExperimentCollectionSnapshot option, ExperimentCollectionError>; listCollections : unit -> Result<CollectionName list, ExperimentCollectionError> }. Provide a mock plus a mock-driven test exercising every field through its exact signature.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub ExperimentCollectionProxy and exercise all three fields through their exact signatures; it passes."}
{"number":29,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-I4","id":"STORE_XDUO_0005","name":"ExperimentCollectionProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[28],"how_to":"Implement ExperimentCollectionProxy.createInMemory closing over a ref Map<CollectionName, ExperimentCollectionSnapshot> (the same createInMemory precedent): saveCollection validates the name and upserts; tryLoadCollection and listCollections read the map. Round-trip unit tests over deterministic data: a collection holding a full E1 setup, a sample-less E2, and a dark E3 — with and without DataFilePath attachments — saves, lists, and loads value-identically.","acceptance":"After the step, in-memory round-trips preserve ordered setups, optional sample/source shapes including the dark experiment, and DataFilePath attachments — unit-verified."}
{"number":30,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-J1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3,18],"how_to":"Extend the renderer input Drawable (Ui/ElementRenderer.fs after the move; today TestWindows/ElementRenderer.fs:26-32) with bindingState : BindingState where BindingState = BoundElement | UnboundElement | NotBindableElement. The host computes it from placement.valueId — bound when Some; Lens, FlatMirror, and CurvedMirror are NotBindableElement and render normally (Placement.fs:93-101). UnboundElement draws a DASHED outline with a ghosted (reduced-opacity) fill — a PATTERN difference, not a hue difference (colorblind-safe); BoundElement stays solid as today; the readout and Details bay keep stating the binding in text. Headless render tests: an unbound sample renders dashed and ghosted, a pre-bound polarizer renders solid, a lens renders normally — one frame each without throwing.","acceptance":"After the step, headless frames MUST show dashed-and-ghosted unbound elements, solid bound elements, and normal not-bindable elements, with the Details text unchanged.","section":"Part J — Table visuals: binding state and out-of-band"}
{"number":31,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-J2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Tests","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[25,30],"how_to":"Add the out-of-band diagnostic, independent of bound/unbound. A PURE Domain function: given an element's binding, the materials reachable through it (a sample's layer material versions; a directly bound material), and the wavelengths THE ACTUAL EXPERIMENT REQUESTS (a single lambda for a fixed setting; the full swept range for a wavelength sweep — derived from the step-25 experiment setup or the scene source), it flags when SOME reachable material is dispersive AND the requested set falls partly outside the union of that material's defined dispersion segments (EditSegment.interval, MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:100-102); constant materials NEVER flag; the result carries per-material defined vs requested ranges as typed data. Render a small warning badge on the flagged element with a hover tooltip naming the offending material(s) and both ranges; the same text appears in the Details bay. Unit tests: 600 nm inside a 300-700 nm segment does not flag; a 200-800 nm sweep against the same segment flags; multi-segment unions; constant materials never flag. Headless test: the badge renders on a flagged element.","acceptance":"After the step, a fixed 600 nm request inside a 300-700 nm segment MUST NOT flag while a 200-800 nm sweep MUST flag naming the material with defined vs requested ranges, constant materials never flag, and the badge plus tooltip text render headless."}
{"number":32,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-K1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3],"how_to":"Rework the Material editor layout and preview. Layout: replace the single-column DockPanel arrangement (MaterialEditorView view, today MaterialEditorView.fs:1067-1132) with TWO panes split by a vertical GridSplitter — left: identity rows plus the progressive ladder inside a ScrollViewer (actions/status pinned below); right: the chart area filling the FULL pane height, both panes with sensible minimum widths. Preview: replace the single-curve chart (n/k from sqrt of eps11 only — NkDispersionChart.fs:40-64) with TABBED multi-curve charts: tab 'n, k' — ALL principal axes (n_x/n_y/n_z on the left axis, k_x/k_y/k_z on the right) with a legend and per-series show/hide toggles, extending the builder to per-axis sampling through the same engine getEps path; tab 'Gyration' — g components vs wavelength, PRESENT ONLY when optically active (series assembled through the engine RhoWithDispValue.toRhoWithDisp, OpticalProperties/Active.fs:152); tab 'mu' — Polder components vs wavelength, only when magnetic (MuWithDispValue.toMuWithDisp, Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:671). Tabs appear and disappear with the ladder toggles, so the visible tab plus legend always answer what is being drawn. Charts embed through EmbeddedChart (Controls/EmbeddedChart.fs) and MUST render under the headless ui-smoke frame without throwing; the Materials window view panel reuses the 'n, k' tab builder. Headless tests: the splitter and full-height chart exist; the Gyration and mu tabs track the activity/magnetic toggles; one frame renders per tab for an isotropic, a biaxial, an active, and a magnetic entry.","acceptance":"After the step, the Material editor is a two-pane vertical-splitter layout with a full-height tabbed chart — per-axis n/k always, Gyration exactly when active, mu exactly when magnetic — all rendering headless without throwing.","section":"Part K — Editor rework"}
{"number":33,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-K2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[3],"how_to":"Add unsaved-edit confirmation to BOTH editors. Capture the edit state at load (init) and define dirty = structural inequality between the captured and the current edit state (plain records/DUs; function-valued context fields excluded; no dirty flags to maintain). Intercept BOTH exits: CancelClicked (today MaterialEditorView.fs:423-424 and SampleEditorView.fs:549-550 close silently) and the window chrome via OnClosing on the two HostWindows. When dirty, show a confirm surface offering 'Discard changes' / 'Keep editing' in one row with distinct negative/positive styling; when pristine, close silently as today. Headless tests: pristine cancel closes immediately; an edited editor's Cancel shows the confirm; Keep editing returns to the editor; Discard closes without saving; the OnClosing path is equally gated.","acceptance":"After the step, a dirty editor MUST NOT close silently through Cancel or the window chrome — the Discard/Keep confirm gates both — while a pristine editor closes immediately, verified headless."}
{"number":34,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-L1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[25],"how_to":"Pure measured-data parsers in OpticalConstructor.Domain — text in, values out (the text-taking parser precedent that keeps filesystem IO and exceptions out: SpectralImport.parseSpectrumCsv, OpticalConstructor.Storage/SpectralImport.fs). Types: IntensitySeries and EllipsometricSeries records over elevated point types; ExperimentDataError with cases like MalformedDataFile, EmptyDataFile, DataRangeMismatch, DataUnitsMismatch — each carrying reason : string. Intensity schema v1 (STRICT): first row is labels (ignored), then comma-separated X,Y rows, invariant culture, a typed error naming the first malformed row; the X column MEANS whatever the experiment's varied parameter says. Ellipsometric schema v1: header wavelength_nm, psi_deg, delta_deg with optional aoi_deg, one file per experiment. NO delimiter sniffing, NO unit heuristics, NO NCS or Mueller-element imports — those are future parsers, not schema changes. Add validateAgainstExperiment : series vs a step-25 experiment's varied parameter, range, and detector kind, returning typed range/units mismatches — a LOUD error, never a silent trim. Every test runs against in-memory strings.","acceptance":"After the step, good, malformed, and empty CSV strings parse or reject with typed errors, a range or units mismatch against the experiment yields the typed validation error, and no test performs file IO.","section":"Part L — Inverse wiring (solver out of scope)"}
{"number":35,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-L2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0006","name":"ExperimentDataProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Domain","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[34],"how_to":"Declare in OpticalConstructor.Domain the measured-data load seam: [<ReferenceEquality>] ExperimentDataProxy = { tryLoadIntensity : DataFilePath -> Result<IntensitySeries, ExperimentDataError>; tryLoadEllipsometric : DataFilePath -> Result<EllipsometricSeries, ExperimentDataError> } (DataFilePath from step 25, the series and error types from step 34). Provide a mock (canned series keyed by path) plus a mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests exercising both fields through their exact signatures.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub ExperimentDataProxy and exercise tryLoadIntensity and tryLoadEllipsometric through their exact signatures; it passes."}
{"number":36,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-L2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0006","name":"ExperimentDataProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[35],"how_to":"Implement the thin real-file adapter in OpticalConstructor.Storage — the ONLY new real IO this spec permits (spec-md 0.3c): createFileBacked builds an ExperimentDataProxy whose fields read the file text at the boundary (File.ReadAllText wrapped so any .NET IO exception is caught AT the boundary and mapped to a typed ExperimentDataError case carrying the reason — exceptions never cross into Domain) and delegate to the step-34 pure parsers. Tests: a temp file written under the test output round-trips a known intensity and a known ellipsometric series; a missing path yields the typed error, not a throw; parser semantics stay covered by the step-34 string tests and mocks everywhere else.","acceptance":"After the step, createFileBacked reads a real temp file into the parsed series, maps a missing file to a typed error without throwing, and adds no parsing logic of its own."}
{"number":37,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-L3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[15,25,29,36],"how_to":"Wire the inverse constructor state and the collection builder. Inverse state: an initInverse beside initMainWith (today TestWindows/TableAndElementRotationView.fs:339-358) seeding the scene with the sample element present but UNBOUND (step 30 draws it dashed) or bound to a HINT sample chosen through the Library window's Select state; with NO hint the experiment chart surface is ABSENT; with a hint the chart behaves as today. Collection builder: grow the Experiments bay into named experiment collections — create/rename a collection of step-25 experiments (each possibly sample-less or dark), attach ONE data file per experiment through a file picker whose chosen DataFilePath loads through ExperimentDataProxy (intensity or ellipsometric per the experiment's detector kind) with the per-experiment parse/validation status shown inline as typed messages; collections save/list/load through ExperimentCollectionProxy. Thread the proxies through the App composition mechanically (step 47 owns the composition acceptance). Headless tests over mock proxies: inverse init has an unbound sample and no chart; binding a hint restores the chart; attaching a file records the typed per-experiment status; a collection round-trips through save/list/load.","acceptance":"After the step, the inverse state opens with an unbound sample and no experiment chart, a hint restores the chart, per-experiment file attachment shows typed parse/validation status over mock proxies, and collections round-trip — verified headless."}
{"number":38,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-L4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[37],"how_to":"Wire the inert last-folder setting through the data-file picker. Re-type EnvironmentSettings.lastFolders (Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:184 — persisted but never read or updated by any picker) from string list to Map<string, string> keyed by picker purpose, initially one key for the measured-data picker; the environment loader already falls back to defaults on a shape mismatch (the total-load contract, OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs:33-35), so an old file simply yields an empty map — NO migration code. The picker starts at the persisted folder via FilePickerOpenOptions.SuggestedStartLocation (resolved through the window's StorageProvider — the picker-raising pattern of the retired shell, Ui/Shell.fs:403-414 in today's tree) and UPDATES the stored folder ONLY on a confirmed selection, persisting through UserEnvironment.save; cancel changes nothing. Tests: a confirmed selection updates the purpose-keyed folder; cancel leaves it untouched; the next open passes the persisted folder to the picker options — the option-building logic is a pure function unit-tested without a real picker.","acceptance":"After the step, a confirmed file selection persists the picker's folder under its purpose key, cancel changes nothing, and the next open starts from the persisted folder — with the option-building logic unit-tested purely."}
{"number":39,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-L5","id":"UICOMP_XDUO_0011","name":"SolverHandoffWindow","kind":"component","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Ui","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[29,36,37],"how_to":"Create the inverse flow's terminal screen in OpticalConstructor.Ui, opened from the inverse constructor through WindowLauncher (single instance): it lists GENERAL information about the received collection — each experiment with its ordered setup, detector kind, attached file, and per-file parse/validation status — plus the fixed message that the actual solver will be done separately. It performs basic validation and reports TYPED per-experiment errors: every element except the sample is specified; every experiment has a readable, schema-valid data file (through ExperimentDataProxy); ranges are consistent (step-34 validateAgainstExperiment). NO solving and NO normalization occur — data is gathered raw; corrections belong to the future solver. Stable intent-named ids for the window, the summary list, and each status row. Headless tests over mock proxies: a fully valid collection lists green statuses; a missing file and a range mismatch each show their typed message; no computation beyond validation runs.","acceptance":"After the step, the handoff window summarizes the collection with per-experiment typed validation statuses and the solver-comes-later message, flagging missing files and range mismatches, with no solver math anywhere — verified headless over mocks."}
{"number":40,"anchor":"ADD_COMPONENT","ac":"AC-M1","id":"STORE_XDUO_0007","name":"TestDbContext","kind":"component","language":"csharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Database","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Database","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[5],"how_to":"Create the nearly-empty C# EFC project Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Database (net10.0, x64; add to Berreman.slnx), modeled on the STL migrations shape (Softellect/Apps/DistrProc/Migrations/Common — CommonDbContext.cs and its per-service migrations): ONE Test entity (an int Id key plus a Name column), TestDbContext, and an initial EFC migration. Provider selection (MSSQL vs SQLite, an enumerated choice parsed to a DU on the F# side of the test) and connection strings come from appsettings.json via AppSettingsProvider.tryGetConnectionString and the step-5 ConfigKey entries — never a hardcoded string. Its ONLY purpose is proving EFC wiring creates and migrates; NO product project references it. An OpticalConstructor.Tests F# test references the project and runs Database.Migrate() against SQLite on a temp file under the test output, asserting the Test table exists; no MSSQL server is required anywhere.","acceptance":"After the step, the initial migration creates the Test table against SQLite inside a test, provider and connection string come from appsettings, and no product project references OpticalConstructor.Database.","section":"Part M — Storage scaffolding"}
{"number":41,"anchor":"ADD_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-M2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0008","name":"SeedingProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","declaring_project":"OpticalConstructor.Seeding","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Seeding","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[14],"how_to":"Create the F# class-library project Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Seeding (net10.0, x64; add to Berreman.slnx; references OpticalConstructor.Domain) declaring the seed-push seam: SeedingError = SeedRejected of reason : string; [<ReferenceEquality>] SeedingProxy = { saveCategory : MaterialCategory -> Result<unit, SeedingError>; saveMaterial : MaterialEntry -> Result<unit, SeedingError>; saveSample : Sample -> Result<unit, SeedingError>; saveLibraryEntry : LibraryEntry -> Result<unit, SeedingError> }; and seedAll : SeedingProxy -> Result<unit, SeedingError> pushing the EXISTING Domain seed values — standardCategories (MaterialLibrary.fs:118), builtInEntries (:363), the SeedSamples values (ElementId.fs:381), seedEntries (:532) — in category, material, sample, entry order. The seeds STAY where they live next to their types; seeded Guids are frozen forever (future foreign keys). Mock-driven test in OpticalConstructor.Tests: seedAll over a recording stub receives every seed value exactly once, in order, through the exact signatures.","acceptance":"After the step, a mock-driven test MUST prove seedAll pushes every existing seed value exactly once, in category-material-sample-entry order, through the record's exact signatures; it passes."}
{"number":42,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT","ac":"AC-M2","id":"STORE_XDUO_0008","name":"SeedingProxy","kind":"proxy","language":"fsharp","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Seeding","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[21,22,41],"how_to":"Implement SeedingProxy.createInMemory: adapt the REAL in-memory stores — the add verbs of CategoryProxy, MaterialProxy, SampleProxy and the library entry store — so seeding runs with NO database at all; a future DB cycle swaps only the record's fields. Because the existing createInMemory constructors self-seed, add EMPTY-store constructors in Domain (createInMemoryEmpty beside the seeded ones) for the seeding pipeline — the pipeline is what fills a blank store; the app composition keeps using the self-seeding constructors unchanged. Tests: seedAll over empty stores reproduces the seeded catalogue — category, material, sample, and entry counts match the Domain seed lists and the fixed seed Guids resolve — all Result-checked, no real IO.","acceptance":"After the step, seedAll over empty in-memory stores reproduces the seeded catalogue with matching counts and fixed Guids, Result-checked with no database and no file IO."}
{"number":43,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-N1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.Storage","OpticalConstructor.Tests"],"depends_on":[2],"how_to":"Collapse the two recent-files stores into ONE: keep OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs (the bounded-MRU module with the pure bump invariant and its own recent.json) as the single recent-files mechanism, and REMOVE the EnvironmentSettings.recentFiles field (Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:185) and its default (:241); any consumer surviving the step-2 shell retirement re-points to Storage.RecentFiles. The environment loader's total-load contract keeps old environment.json files loading (the dropped field is ignored) — no migration code. Update tests.","acceptance":"After the step, EnvironmentSettings carries no recentFiles field, Storage.RecentFiles is the only recent-files store in the tree, and build plus tests are green.","section":"Part N — Consolidations, launcher, warnings"}
{"number":44,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-N2","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.TestWindows","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[13,15,39],"how_to":"Consolidate automation ids into ONE [<RequireQualifiedAccess>] module of [<Literal>] intent-named constants (e.g. OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs, compiled first in Controls) with nested per-surface sub-modules (Selector, Materials, Library, FacetedTree, Editors, Launcher, Handoff, and the rest), replacing every per-control UiIds module scattered through Controls and the Ui views. Id VALUES are unchanged — only the declaring module moves — so control sites and tests re-point their references mechanically and no duplicate id literal remains anywhere.","acceptance":"After the step, exactly one module holds every automation-id literal, no per-control UiIds module remains, id values are unchanged, and every headless test still locates its controls."}
{"number":45,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-N3","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[4,13,15,37],"how_to":"Finalize the product launcher (LauncherWindow in OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs, slimmed to Main by step 4): FOUR buttons in THIS order — Main / Inverse / Materials / Library — each with a stable Name and AutomationId. Main opens the constructor as today; Inverse opens the constructor in the step-37 inverse state; Materials and Library open the step-13/15 windows through the app-scoped WindowLauncher, sharing the SAME single instances as constructor-opened ones (the launcher and the constructor share the step-6 app scope). Headless tests: all four buttons present in order; each opens or activates its surface; opening Materials from the launcher and then from the constructor strip yields ONE window.","acceptance":"After the step, the launcher shows Main/Inverse/Materials/Library in order, each button opens its surface over the shared app scope, and Materials opened from launcher then constructor activates one single instance — verified headless."}
{"number":46,"anchor":"IMPLEMENT","ac":"AC-N4","touches":["OpticalConstructor.Ui","OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Controls","OpticalConstructor.Domain","OpticalConstructor.Storage"],"depends_on":[44,45],"how_to":"Sweep the build warning-clean per spec-md 0.6: dotnet build Berreman.slnx -c Release MUST emit no FS warning originating in our code and no MSBuild warning from our project configuration — in particular MSB3277 must not have been reintroduced by the relocation or the three new projects. Fix every finding at its source (types, references, project configuration), never with a suppression attribute or NoWarn. Only the exempt third-party NuGet advisories (NU1701, NU1901-NU1904) may remain.","acceptance":"After the step, a Release build of Berreman.slnx completes with zero our-code FS or MSBuild warnings, with only the exempt NU1701/NU1901-NU1904 advisories remaining."}
{"number":47,"anchor":"WIRE_UI","ac":"AC-W1","touches":["OpticalConstructor.App","OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"],"depends_on":[8,13,15,27,29,36,39,40,42,45,46],"how_to":"Finalize the composition root in OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs: create the AppSettingsProvider once and materialize the typed settings record (step 5); build the app scope (step 6) with the five stores plus SceneProxy.createInMemory (step 27), ExperimentCollectionProxy.createInMemory (step 29), and the file-backed ExperimentDataProxy (step 36); construct the WindowRegistry and WindowLauncher with every window factory — Materials, Library, the three editors, SolverHandoff — and the modality switch; hand the whole context to the launcher window and both constructor states. Drive the entire surface headless in Ui.Tests: the ui-smoke suite renders one frame each for the launcher, the Main constructor, the Inverse constructor, the Materials and Library windows in Browse and Select states, the three editor windows, and the SolverHandoff window without throwing.","acceptance":"After composition, every proxy and the launcher seam are built exactly once at the root, the ui-smoke suite renders launcher, both constructor states, both faceted windows in both modes, the three editors, and the handoff window without throwing, and every test gate is at or above its baseline count."}
